 the kitchen  and that he couldn't come in or he would  mess it up completely  then i got to work at first all i had to  go on was a handwritten ingredient list  that i found  years ago i have a 25 year old piece of  paper with my dad's  nearly illegible handwriting on it it's  not like a full  step-by-step recipe it's sort of just a  collection of ingredients  i've started by chopping some onions  really finely  chopping some carrots so i'm putting  some water on  to boil back there what i've never  pureed anything i'm the least qualified  person to do this but  i am determined too mango is actually  the first food i  ever ate look at that  half a cup exactly  oh yeah those are some liquefied carrots  so the special ingredient to  this hot sauce is this blend of spices  here that i'm not going to tell you  what's in it but let me just tell you it  smells  wonderful it's time for the peppers got  my rubber gloves on to make sure  i don't get too much hotness all over me  more than i already have  whoa that's some spicy air hot pepper  puree  oh  really letting these flavors get to know  each other in here  oh something is very wrong with this i'm  gonna have to start over  when that recipe failed i realized that  i had to dig deeper so i went back  into his paperwork and kept searching  while i was there  i found a lot of very interesting stuff  i found the business card of the man who  conned him i found  the catalog he told me about i found all  sorts of things that corroborated this  story and the fact that he was holding  on to these things decades later  showed me that this really did hurt him  most importantly though  i found a real recipe a recipe for a  large batch  which includes six five gallon buckets  of  peppers might be a little much but what  i can do is i can take  this and i can convert it down to  something a bit more manageable  yesterday i was using as much vinegar  and lime juice as pretty much every  other ingredient which  definitely made it a bit more acidic  than i wanted so today  when i've converted everything down it  does cut  a significant amount of that acidity out  the other thing about this recipe is  that it says to use  canned peaches crossing my fingers for a  successful second batch  this time it had to work i was running  out of peppers and that was the one  ingredient that i couldn't get any more  of  take two mango  next up are the peaches  carrot time so onions  throw that in there third a cup of lime  juice  spice mix  the blade  now all that's left is to grind up some  that's peppers here we go  oh please please please be good  that is so much better yes  so it tasted good to me but i had no  idea whether or not it was authentic for  that i would have to give it to  my dad but i wanted to make the  experience as authentic as possible  so along with one of his old bottles i  actually found a roll of his old labels  and  i knew that would be the icing on the  cake of surprising him with this  this is the final product mango creek's  hot sauce  i'm about to give it to my dad do you  think he knows  he's suspicious for sure hey hey  what's happening i have something for  you  [Music]  uh how could you where where the hell  could you get this  i found the recipe i got the peppers  from a caribbean grocery store in new  york  and i i made it and you found my old  lady i found your old labels  wow dakota yeah that is absolutely  unbelievable it looks exactly like it  did  you want to try it yeah i'd love to  maybe a little chunky that's exactly  like it was exactly how it used to be  that's a lot  oh my god it's delicious does it taste  like it should  exactly i feel like i messed up a little  bit but  it was as good as i could get it it's  supposed to be hot  i just love the flavor yeah it's very  nice  you're amazing i cannot believe you did  this how long has it been since you had  that  [Music]  97 98 wow okay  well this is amazing i mean  makes my heart sore because you know  this is what i did my dad has done a lot  since we left charleston he's worked in  stores been a sous chef made maple syrup  and he's even publishing a book in  november  link in the description but this hot  sauce has always been  a part of his identity just one that i'd  never really  uncovered i was born in charleston but  when i was about a month old my family  moved back to vermont  so their time there always seemed  separate from me like  a story that i was told but i was never  part of  thank you joy  so it was amazing to be able to bring a  bit of that story back and to be a part  of it i feel really lucky that i was  able to do this for him now and  who knows maybe it'll make him get back  into it  [Music]  you

